<p>1) What you have under &quot;Central Narrative&quot; should actually go under &quot;Page Type&quot;. The Hook and Elevator Pitch are fine.</p>
<p>2) Kill the Additional Notes; if you're not sure it's a friendly dog and you're the one writing it, then you're wasting people's time. Decide one way or another.</p>
<p>3) SCP-2137 usually only worries about serial killers or other major criminals. If the dog is mentioned by it, then there needs to an actual reason for it, and that should be interesting.</p>
<p>4) The story behind the St. Bernard needs some serious work. Prior history would be nice, such as how long it has been around, some theories as to how it gained its abilities, and even some stories about why it does what it does. We need some details, and there aren't any here.</p>

